We are given 54 cards dealt equally to \(x\) players, so \(x \cdot y = 54\) with \(x, y\) integers. Constraints: \(x \ge 2\) and \(y \ge 5\). Since \(y = 54/x \ge 5\), we have \(x \le 54/5 = 10.8\), so \(x \le 10\).

The divisors of 54 are: 1, 2, 3, 6, 9, 18, 27, 54. Filtering those satisfying \(2 \le x \le 10\) gives \(x = 2, 3, 6, 9\). For each, \(y\) is \(\ge 5\) (27, 18, 9, 6 respectively). Thus there are 4 possible values of \(x\).

\boxed{4}

